            <ArticleTitle>Effect of Skin Application of Dorogov's Antiseptic-Stimulant on Behavioral Reactions in Rats.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>677-680</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s10517-017-3877-9</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Local application of the Dorogov's antiseptic-stimulant onto the skin of 2-month-old male Sprague-Dawley rats in a low dose (0.5 g/kg/day) for 1 week increased motor and ultrasonic activity of experimental animals and the content of activated c-Fos+ neurons on the cingular, motor, insular, and pyriform cortex and in the striatum.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
